# ==============================================================================
# GHAADD - Core .gitignore Setup
# ==============================================================================

# --- 1. Python Cache & Compilation Artifacts ---
__pycache__/
modules/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- 2. Volatile Daemon Runtime & Status States ---
ghaadd.lock
ghaadd.daemon.status.json
ghaadd.daemon.status.json.*.tmp
ghaadd.daemon.stderr.log
perf_baseline*.json
mapping.json.lock
mapping.json.*.tmp
mapping.json.v1.bak*

# --- 3. SQLite Local Write Records & Engine Caches ---
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# --- 4. Environment Variables & Credentials ---
.env

# --- 5. AI Workspace Exclusions ---
CLAUDE.md

# --- 6. Local and personal config files ---
config.json
mapping.json

# --- 7. Misc files ---
ToDo.txt

# ==============================================================================
# NOTES (about AI):
#
# Claude commands:
# /usage
# /clear.
# /compact
#
# Reset (/clear):
# This wipes the conversation history entirely while keeping your project
# structure and your local CLAUDE.md instructions perfectly intact. When your
# limits reset, you start at zero tokens, completely bypassing the threat of an
# expired cache.
#
# Auto-Compacting Trigger (/compact):
# As you approach your context threshold, Claude Code will automatically run an
# background compression routine (/compact) on your chat log. It tries to shrink
# the chat history into a dense summary so the agent doesn't crash from a memory
# overflow.
#
# The Side Effect:
# While the underlying AI logic isn't trying to wrap up early, the loss of
# fine-grained history from that automated compression can cause Claude to lose
# track of minor details from 20 prompts ago. It might feel like it's rushing or
# missing instructions, but it is a byproduct of memory management, not a
# deliberate throttling of quality.
#
# The "Token Trap":
# While auto-resume sounds incredibly useful, the developer community has
# identified a significant financial/token penalty to leaving it on:
# Because the system sits idle for hours waiting for the limit to clear, your
# prompt cache will expire. When the session auto-resumes, Claude has to re-read
# your entire codebase context and session history completely from scratch.
# Users have reported that the very first "auto-resume" message can instantly
# eat up a massive portion of the newly refreshed 5-hour token budget right off
# the bat.
# ==============================================================================
